## 4. XML Report Format (Read Before Writing parse_reports.py)

Each report in `data/raw/reports/` is an XML file structured like this:

```xml
<MedlineCitation>
  <Abstract>
    <AbstractText Label="FINDINGS">Mild cardiomegaly. No pneumothorax.</AbstractText>
    <AbstractText Label="IMPRESSION">No acute cardiopulmonary disease.</AbstractText>
  </Abstract>
  <parentImage id="CXR1234_IM-0001-1001"/>
  <parentImage id="CXR1234_IM-0001-2001"/>
</MedlineCitation>
```

**What to extract from each XML:**
- `findings` — text content of `AbstractText Label="FINDINGS"`
- `impression` — text content of `AbstractText Label="IMPRESSION"`
- `image_ids` — all `parentImage id` attributes

**How image IDs map to filenames:**
The `id` attribute maps directly to a PNG filename:
```
parentImage id="CXR1234_IM-0001-1001"  →  data/raw/images/CXR1234_IM-0001-1001.png
```

One report links to one or more images (typically 2: frontal + lateral).
Use the frontal view for the CNN input. If you can't distinguish frontal from lateral
by filename, use the first image ID as the default.

