## 9. Schemas

### `studies.csv`
```
study_id, image_path, report_text, findings, impression
```
`study_id` maps to the XML filename (e.g. `0001` for `0001.xml`).
`image_path` points to the primary (frontal) PNG in `data/raw/images/`.

### `retrieval_chunks.csv`
```
chunk_id, study_id, chunk_text, section
```
`section`: "findings" or "impression".

### `RadiologyReport` pydantic schema
```python
class RadiologyReport(BaseModel):
    findings:   str
    impression: str
    rationale:  str
    caution:    str
    escalate:   bool
    confidence: Literal["high", "moderate", "low"]
```

### POST /predict
```json
// request
{ "image_path": "data/raw/images/CXR123.png", "clinical_indication": "shortness of breath" }

// response
{
  "predictions": [{"label": "Edema", "prob": 0.79}, {"label": "Pleural Effusion", "prob": 0.73}],
  "retrieved_evidence": [{"chunk_id": "c88", "text": "Bilateral interstitial...", "score": 0.84}],
  "summary": {
    "findings": "Bilateral interstitial opacities with small pleural effusions.",
    "impression": "Pattern may reflect pulmonary edema / CHF.",
    "rationale": "Evidence chunks 1–2 describe similar bilateral opacities in CHF context.",
    "caution": "Model output is for research use only. Not validated for clinical use.",
    "escalate": false, "confidence": "moderate"
  }
}
```

